### Requests for the IntelliJ HTTP client (or copy them as curl commands).
### Start the app first: ./mvnw spring-boot:run

### List all users
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users

### Create a user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ada",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "fullName": "Ada Lovelace"
}

### Get one user (exercise in step 04)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/1

### Delete a user
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/users/1

### Step 06: invalid input -> 400 Bad Request
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "",
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

### Step 06: same email twice -> 409 Conflict (run "Create a user" first)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ada2",
  "email": "ada@example.com"
}

### Step 06: unknown id -> 404 Not Found
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/999
